      "name": "theme-base",
      "note": "/* ── Dark: the default. A deep violet ground — the app's own color, taken\n   from the mark; surfaces climb by LIGHTNESS, borders do the separating,\n   shadows only mark true depth.\n   PURPLE IS THE GROUND, NOT THE ACCENT. That is a measured decision, not a\n   taste: `#8b5cf6` as an accent scores 4.20:1 on `--panel` and fails the\n   4.5 floor, and every lavender that passes is the same hue as the ground,\n   so it stops reading as \"live\". Teal stays the accent and scores BETTER\n   here than it did on the old blue-steel (9.96:1 vs 9.75:1) because teal\n   and violet are near-complementary. See DESIGN-SYSTEM §3. ─────────────── */",
